            "review_title": "Review at Noi Kitchen & Bar",
            "review_text": "Abocadosalada\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam13 contributions\n3\nHidden gem with great menu\nFeb 2019 • Solo\nDefinitely my go to place for a lone meal with great variation of comfort food. Noi is one of the very few, if not the only restaurant that serves multiple cuisine and manages to nail all of them. I was extremely hesitated the first time looking at the menu, but after multiple come backs I have tried the chicken tender (with addictive sauce),chili con carne, pan fried sea bass with ratatouille, chicken and mozzarella pot, roasted chicken breast with mushroom sauce and pasta, the crispy Vietnamese garlic fried rice and seafood...and they are all so good I was left eager to come back for more. And the menu doesn't just stop there, they have a selection of special dishes that changes every day and is always super fun and refreshing as well. On the other side, dessert menu is quite limited but I'm happy with the lava cake that I get everytime.\nPrice: This is the only Western restaurant in Thao Dien I've seen with all the main courses cost less than 200k. In an area where a breakfast can easily cost you 250k this is an incredibly good deal for cheap eaters (or just sensible eaters).\nAmbience: one thing I love about Noi is that it's always super quiet (if you seat indoors). Everytime I came there was just only me inside the restaurant, with a large group of frquent customers, mostly French, eating and chatting happily on the outdoor benches. Sometimes there's a party at night on the second floor but there's always just one or two tables in the main dining hall. It seems like the owner has already built a large and stable group of loyal customers and doesn't want to push the marketing (hence 8 reviews on TripAdvisor lol) but I believe some exposure wouldn't harm.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 31, 2019",
